kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "debug-log"
purpose: "Debug 观察管线：env 驱动激活的 tracing 文件日志（~/.xylitol/logs/xylitol.log），file-only 不毁 TUI 渲染，在组合根 app::cli::run 统一装配，激活既有 infra/agent 埋点。"
valid_scope[1]: src/app/cli/logging.rs
requirements[1]{req_id,title,statement}:
  dl1,"debug-observation-pipeline","The application MUST activate a tracing subscriber that writes ONLY to a file (~/.xylitol/logs/xylitol.log), NEVER to stdout or stderr, so that TUI rendering (Viewport::Inline + raw mode + per-frame DSR cursor query) is never corrupted by log output. The subscriber MUST be installed exactly once at the composition root (app::cli::run, right after CliArgs::parse and before any mode dispatch), covering all app surfaces (print, TUI, RPC, subcommands). Activation MUST be environment-driven only with no CLI flag and no settings field: when RUST_LOG is set the subscriber installs with EnvFilter::try_from_default_env(); else when XYLITOL_DEBUG=1 it installs with a default filter; otherwise NO subscriber is installed and all tracing macros are no-op with zero overhead. The file writer MUST be synchronous (std::fs::OpenOptions append, NOT tracing-appender non_blocking) so that panic=abort cannot drop buffered log lines, and the file MUST be created with mode 0o600 on unix. The writer MUST disable ANSI (with_ansi(false)). Existing tracing emit sites in infra/ and agent/ MUST become observable automatically without code changes to those layers. The TUI layer MUST only call tracing:: macros (e.g. tracing::debug!) and MUST NOT import infra or install any subscriber (layering invariant). Evidence: tracing 0.1.44 is already an unconditional dependency and ~12 tracing::warn!/info!/debug! call sites already exist across infra (event, permission, mcp, settings, hooks) and agent (compaction), but no tracing_subscriber init and no RUST_LOG reference exist anywhere in the repo, so these emits are entirely silent today; the TUI layer has zero tracing calls."
scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  dl1,"no-subscriber-by-default",neither RUST_LOG nor XYLITOL_DEBUG is set,the app is launched in any mode (print or tui),"no tracing subscriber is installed, no log file is created under ~/.xylitol/logs/, and all tracing:: macros execute as no-ops with no observable behavior change versus before this change"
  dl1,"file-only-never-stdout-stderr",RUST_LOG or XYLITOL_DEBUG is set and the TUI is active,"a tracing::debug! event is emitted from any layer",the event is written to ~/.xylitol/logs/xylitol.log and nothing is written to stdout or stderr so the inline viewport and DSR cursor query are not corrupted
  dl1,"rust-log-controls-level",RUST_LOG is set to a specific directive,a tracing event matching (or not matching) the directive is emitted,"EnvFilter::try_from_default_env governs whether the event is recorded (the explicit RUST_LOG directive wins over the XYLITOL_DEBUG default filter)"
  dl1,"xylitol-debug-one-switch",XYLITOL_DEBUG=1 is set and RUST_LOG is unset,the app is launched,"the subscriber installs with the default filter (xylitol=debug,warn) and a tracing::debug! from the xylitol crate appears in the log file"
